From king at harvard.edu  Tue Jul 12 12:10:42 2005
From: king at harvard.edu (Gary King)
Date: Tue, 12 Jul 2005 12:10:42 -0400 (EDT)
Subject: [amelia] two queries
In-Reply-To: <20050712151549.73298.qmail@web53301.mail.yahoo.com>
References: <20050712151549.73298.qmail@web53301.mail.yahoo.com>
Message-ID: <Pine.LNX.4.63.0507121209170.12012@w3.hmdc.harvard.edu>


yes, variables need to be identified if they're nominal, or else the 
algorithm will treat them as if they're continuous.  The latter isn't 
really much of a problem in practice in many cases except where the 
nominal categories aren't also ordered.  So dichotomies and ordered 
categories seem to work ok.  The manual has more info on this.

Gary

